---
import ResourceCard from '../../../components/ResourceCard.astro';
import Button from '../../../components/Button.astro';
import DocumentLayout from '../../../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
import ContentCard from '../../../components/ContentCard.astro';
import catalog from '../../../../public/graphs/working/event-profiles/catalog.json';
import validation from '../../../../public/graphs/working/event-profiles/validation.json';
const domains = ['Identity','Host','Network','Cloud','Email','Application','File'];
---
<DocumentLayout title="Event profiles" description="Explicit event contexts and evidence walkthroughs across all seven TENSOR investigation domains." canonicalPath="/graphs/profiles/">
  <ContentCard>
    <p class="section-kicker">Same graph · explicit event contexts</p>
    <h2>Investigate the event you actually have.</h2>
    <p>State changes, mailbox rules and autonomous actions need their own subjects and evidence. These <strong>{Object.keys(catalog.profiles).length} public draft profiles</strong> add those contexts above the complete 609-question graph. Follow {validation.scenarioCount} authored investigation routes, including contradicted hypotheses, unavailable evidence, independent fallback and coverage gaps.</p>
    <p><strong>{catalog.version} · author-tested draft.</strong> Each profile publishes distinct, qualified question identities. The base graph, schema, published releases and frozen review package are unchanged. External domain review and independent exchange remain open.</p>
    <div class="profile-domain-list">{domains.map(domain => <section aria-label={`${domain} event profiles`}><h3>{domain}</h3><div class="profile-cards">{Object.entries(catalog.profiles).filter(([,p])=>p.domain===domain).map(([id,p])=><ResourceCard class="profile-card" href={`/graphs/profiles/${id}/`} title={p.title}><p>{p.proposition}</p><small>Bind {p.bindings.join(' · ')}</small></ResourceCard>)}</div></section>)}</div>
    <h2>Keep the distinctions visible</h2>
    <p>A snapshot does not establish a historical change. A requested or failed action does not prove success. A missing file does not prove deletion; unlink does not prove secure erasure. Unavailable content stays unknown for content-based hypotheses. Every relationship target retains its own profile, subjects, evidence and time context.</p>
    <p>These are plausible investigations using fictitious identifiers and supplied assessed observations. They do not authenticate production evidence, demonstrate universal coverage or grant authority to act.</p>
    <p><a href="/graphs/working/event-profiles/README.md">Profile contract and limits</a> · <a href="/graphs/working/event-profiles/catalog.json" download>Catalog</a> · <a href="/graphs/working/event-profiles/definitions.json" download>Qualified definitions</a> · <a href="/graphs/working/event-profiles/scenarios.json" download>Scenario evidence</a> · <a href="/graphs/working/event-profiles/validation.json" download>Validation and source pins</a></p>
    <p><Button variant="secondary" href="/graphs/">Explore the base graph</Button> <Button variant="secondary" href="/graphs/coverage/">Original-question coverage ledger</Button></p>
  </ContentCard>
</DocumentLayout>
<style>
.profile-domain-list { display: grid; gap: 1.4rem; margin: 2rem 0; }
h3 { color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: .6rem; }
.profile-cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,16rem),1fr)); gap: .6rem; }
.profile-card small { font-size: .7rem; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
